er the Aspen Acres burn scar.\n\n* WHERE...Aspen Acres Burn Scar\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Aspen Acres burn scar is expected\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Aspen\nAcres burn scar should prepare for potential debris flow. Be sure\nto stay up to date with information from local authorities. Heavy\nrainfall could trigger flash flooding of low-lying areas, street\nflooding, and debris flows in and near recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weather Service Meteorologists are forecasting\nthunderstorms with heavy rainfall over the burn scar, which may\nlead to flash flooding and debris flows.\n- Some locations that may experience flash flooding include...\nBeulah, San Isabel, and highways 165 and 78 in and around the\nAspen Acres Burn Scar.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-16T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.31c19b6bbaf8561e4971d908ab5f9bc2adbb967c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.31c19b6bbaf8561e4971d908ab5f9bc2adbb967c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-17T00:07:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 170007 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 607 PM MDT Sun Aug 16 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Showers and storms continue this evening, some strong to severe. Strong winds, hail, and heavy rain/flash flooding on the table. - Afternoon storms are expected again on Monday, mostly over the eastern mountains and Raton Mesa. - A bit drier through the rest of th","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-16T17:21:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 161721 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1